### LLM-as-Judge Calibration

Before using the LLM judge for reply-quality evaluation, we calibrated it against
8 examples manually reviewed by a human.

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Calibration examples | 8 |
| Exact score agreement | 25.0% |
| Agreement within ±1 point | 87.5% |
| Human mean score | 3.75/5 |
| LLM judge mean score | 5.00/5 |

The calibration revealed an important limitation: the LLM judge was consistently
more optimistic than the human reviewer. It assigned 5/5 to all eight examples,
while the human scores ranged from 2/5 to 5/5.

Therefore, the LLM judge is treated as a supporting evaluation signal rather
than ground truth. Human review is necessary for calibration and for interpreting
the automated quality scores.